{"step_index":173,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:29:04Z","input_tokens":12386,"cache_read_tokens":75781,"output_tokens":1777,"content":"# 🛡️ NexusMobility — Complete Code Audit, Bug Fix & Hardening Report\n\nA comprehensive engineering audit across the entire codebase ([`app.js`](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/app.js), [`styles.css`](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/styles.css), and [`index.html`](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/index.html)) has been conducted. All detected runtime bugs, edge-case risks, rendering leaks, and state synchronization issues have been systematically resolved.\n\n---\n\n## 🔍 1. Bug Report & Audit Summary\n\n| ID | Module / Area | Issue Description | Severity | Fix Applied |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **BUG-01** | `app.js` (`findOptimalEcoRoute`) | **Missing Disconnected Node & Loop Safety**: In edge cases where stations were disconnected or invalid IDs passed, `dist[endId]` resulted in `Infinity` and path extraction could fail or loop. | **Critical** | Added strict checks: verify start/end presence, check `dist[endId] !== Infinity`, guard loop iterations with `path.length <= TRANSIT_STATIONS.length`, and return structured zero-cost result for identical or unreachable nodes. |\n| **BUG-02** | `app.js` (`Urban3DCanvas` & `AmbientEcoCanvas`) | **Unbounded Animation Loops & Memory Leak**: `requestAnimationFrame` continued running unconditionally in background tabs even when the canvas was hidden, causing unnecessary CPU/GPU usage. | **Major** | Implemented `pause()` and `resume()` hooks on canvas instances, hooked into tab switching (`initTabNavigation`), and stored `animId` with clean `cancelAnimationFrame`. |\n| **BUG-03** | `app.js` (`Urban3DCanvas.drawAnimatedCar`) | **Potential `NaN` Heading Vector & Coordinate Overflow**: When adjacent waypoints projected to the exact same screen pixel, `Math.atan2(0, 0)` could yield `0` or indeterminate angles; negative camera $Z$ could cause division by zero. | **Major** | Added `Math.max(10, cameraDist + z2)` camera perspective clamp and guarded `dx === 0 && dy === 0` before computing `atan2`. Also wrapped dynamic `createLinearGradient` in a fallback `try/catch`. |\n| **BUG-04** | `app.js` (`Urban3DCanvas.resize`) | **Canvas Scale Multiplier Leak**: Calling `ctx.scale` on repeated resize events caused cumulative DPI multiplication. | **Major** | Standardized to `ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0)` on every resize. |\n| **BUG-05** | `app.js` (`revertLatestConfirmation` & `cancelActiveTrip`) | **Driver Seat Capacity Drift & Reference Mutation**: Reverting a dispatch confirmation or canceling a trip could mutate the original passenger object in place or increment driver seats past `originalSeats`. | **Major** | Enforced immutable cloning (`{ ...passenger, status: '...' }`) upon dispatch. Added strict seat clamping: `driver.seats = Math.min(driver.originalSeats, driver.seats + 1)`. |\n| **BUG-06** | `app.js` (`pushToStandby` & `popFromStandby`) | **Boundary Capacity Check**: `pushToStandby` checked `== standbyCap` instead of `>= standbyCap`. | **Minor** | Changed to `this.standbyCount >= this.standbyCap`, guaranteeing ring buffer index wrap-around integrity. |\n| **BUG-07** | `app.js` & `index.html` (Modals) | **Missing ESC Key & Backdrop Click Handlers**: Enterprise confirmation modals could only be dismissed via explicit button clicks, trapping keyboard and mobile users. | **Minor** | Added global `Escape` key event listener and backdrop click listener to dismiss any open modal cleanly. |\n| **BUG-08** | `app.js` (DOM & XSS) | **XSS & Direct String Injection in Renderers**: User-entered passenger and driver names were concatenated directly into `innerHTML` without HTML entity escaping. | **Major** | Added `escapeHTML()` sanitization utility across all dynamic renderers (`renderPassengerDispatchStream`, `renderFleetDirectory`, `renderActiveTrips`, modals, and receipts). |\n| **BUG-09** | `styles.css` (Stacking & Overlays) | **Modal Overlay Z-Index & Print Layout**: Toast container had `z-index: 9999` while modals had `z-index: 1000`, causing toasts to float above active modal dialogs. Also lacked print styles for the Eco-Receipt. | **Minor** | Updated modal overlay `z-index` to `10000`, toast container to `99999`, and added `@media print` styles for clean physical receipts. |\n\n---\n\n## 🛠️ 2. Corrected & Hardened Files\n\nThe updated, production-hardened files are written in place:\n- 📄 [**`app.js`**](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/app.js): Full source code with defensive boundary logic, null-checks, sanitization, and frame control.\n- 🎨 [**`styles.css`**](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/styles.css): Complete CSS with corrected z-indexes, responsive breakpoints, and print styles.\n\n---\n\n## 🧪 3. Verification & Testing Steps\n\n1. **Disconnected / Same-Station Pathfinding**:\n   - In Tab 1 (*Eco-Route Finder*), select **Tech Park Alpha** as both Origin and Destination.\n   - Click **Calculate Route** &rarr; Verifies toast warning: *\"Origin and Destination stations cannot be identical\"* without crash or infinite loops.\n2. **Circular Standby Lounge Boundary**:\n   - In Tab 2 (*Passenger Hub*), click **Push Front Commuter to Standby** repeatedly until 5/5 slots are occupied.\n   - Click once more &rarr; Verifies rejection toast: *\"Priority Standby Lounge is currently at maximum capacity (5/5)\"*, with passenger restored safely to the front.\n3. **Dispatch & Seat Capacity Reversal**:\n   - In Tab 3 (*Driver Console*), onboard a driver with 2 seats.\n   - Dispatch 2 trips &rarr; Seat counter reaches 0/2.\n   - Click **Revert Last Confirmation** &rarr; Restores 1 seat (1/2) and safely re-queues commuter without exceeding original capacity.\n4. **Modal Backdrop & ESC Dismissal**:\n   - Trigger a dispatch modal or view an Eco-Receipt.\n   - Press the <kbd>ESC</kbd> key or click outside the white card on the dark backdrop &rarr; Modal closes instantly.\n5. **Animation Efficiency**:\n   - Switch between tabs &rarr; The 3D map canvas automatically pauses its render loop when not in view, resuming seamlessly when the Route Finder tab is reactivated."}
